  "surprise": "Systems mechanism falsified: 3,540/3,542/3,548 steps vs 136's 3,370 (+5%; 188 vs 180 steps per 15 s), so batching the 30-matrix Newton-Schulz into 4 groups, removing the per-step host sync and fusing AdamW bought almost nothing; the ~80 ms step is GPU-bound, not CPU-dispatch-bound, and the padding waste (batch max ~400 tokens vs mean 135) is the real lead (146-claude's packing tests it). Metric 646/637/633 (mean 639) vs 136's 655/673/646 (658): round-4 RL solved 1147/1089/1125 (mean 1120) and held-out greedy 0.971/0.960/0.974 match 136 (1102/1114/1124; 0.965), so the -19 is eval noise around an unchanged model, not a regression from the different RNG stream. The batched muon_step is a correct drop-in (bitwise-equal on non-transposed shapes, bf16-order noise on transposed) worth reviving only when a bigger or looped model makes the Muon loop a real cost.",
